### Page 1 of 1

```text
RESOLUTION NO._______
ENTITILED:  “A
RESOLUTION
AUTHORIZING
THE
CREATION
AND
APPOINTMENT OF A NEW REED AVENUE CORRIDOR STEERING
COMMITTEE.”
WHEREAS, the development of the Reed Avenue Corridor was selected as a goal of the
governing body during goal setting for 2022; and
WHEREAS, the development of the Reed Avenue Corridor and the West Edge are
significant to the economic development of Cheyenne; and
WHEREAS, multiple investors in real estate along the Reed Avenue Corridor are
concerned regarding the status of the corridor design efforts and legal issues with the Burlington
Northern Railroad; and
WHEREAS, the previous steering committee on this project ceased to meet in December
of 2020; and
WHEREAS, the steering committee will be charged with reviewing all pertinent
documents and reports, holding public meetings, and making recommendations to the governing
body as to the legal and financial considerations involved in the right-of-way acquisition issues
with the Burlington Northern Railroad; and
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, the creation of a new Reed Avenue Corridor steering committee
be created and appoint the following members:  Deputy City Engineer, Wes Bay; Planner II; Mark
Christensen; Ward I Councilman and Downtown Development Authority Board Member; Pete
Laybourn; Wyoming Department of Transportation Systems, Planning & Railroads; Dan Kline;
and, Reed Avenue investors: Tony Lucero; Dave Teubner; and, Misha Westby.
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that this resolution shall be
effective upon passage and execution by the Mayor and City Clerk.
PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED THIS ______DAY OF _____

, 2022
CITY OF CHEYENNE
BY:

Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)
ATTEST:

Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
By Stefanie Boster at 9:41 am, May 18, 2022
```
